invariant: INV-26
file: quic_keys.c
catches: test/lint-quic-surface.sh
reason: quic_keys.c reaches the body of aes_public_key through a macro that
  expands to the header's name, so the directive carries no literal
  include of quic_aes_key.h. A check that matched the quoted include
  text exactly read straight past it while the preprocessor did not.
  tools/quic-footprint.py's key_holders() matches the header's name in
  an include directive however it is spelled, and in the define that
  builds one, and `make lint-quic-surface` is where it runs.

--- old
#include "quic_keys.h"
--- new
#include "quic_keys.h"
#define CH_KEY_BODY "quic_aes_key.h"
#include CH_KEY_BODY
